<Project>
  <!-- Sembazuru MSBuild / Visual Studio integration (M6.2).

       Routes every C/C++ compile through the Sembazuru agent daemon by pointing
       MSBuild's CL task at the `sembazuru` launcher shim (CLToolExe/CLToolPath).
       This is the MSBuild equivalent of CMAKE_<LANG>_COMPILER_LAUNCHER for the
       CMake/Ninja path — no project-file edits, just this drop-in.

       Setup (minimal config):
         1. Copy this file to your solution/repo root as `Directory.Build.targets`.
         2. Before running msbuild, set:
              SEMBAZURU_LAUNCHER_DIR = directory containing sembazuru.exe
              SEMBAZURU_SHIM_CC      = the real compiler ("cl.exe" or "clang-cl.exe")
              SEMBAZURU_DAEMON       = daemon endpoint (default npipe://Sembazuru.LocalIntake.v1)
              SEMBAZURU_INPUT_ROOT   = your solution/repo root (see below)
            and start a daemon + at least one worker (see docs/integrations).

       The launcher hands each compile to the daemon, which distributes it; if the
       daemon is unreachable it falls back to a normal local compile, so the build
       always completes. Set SEMBAZURU_DISABLE=true to bypass the shim entirely.

       Action caching across the MSBuild CL task (SEMBAZURU_INPUT_ROOT):
         MSBuild batches all sources into ONE `cl @<response-file>` invocation, and
         a /Zi build writes objects (obj\) and a shared PDB (bin\) in *separate*
         subtrees. For the action cache to key on the right sources and republish
         every output on a hit, point SEMBAZURU_INPUT_ROOT at the one directory that
         contains them all — your solution/repo root. The launcher anchors the
         response file and the cache relativizes/publishes obj\ and bin\ under this
         single root. Leave it unset to fall back to each compile's own working
         directory (correct, but a /Zi build whose outputs land outside that dir is
         simply not cached — never miscached). A `.sembazuru\` folder of
         content-addressed response files is created under the root; add it to
         .gitignore.

       This file is imported after the C++ toolset (Directory.Build.targets is the
       last import), so it overrides the toolset's default CL.exe. -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(SEMBAZURU_DISABLE)' != 'true' and '$(SEMBAZURU_LAUNCHER_DIR)' != ''">
    <CLToolPath>$(SEMBAZURU_LAUNCHER_DIR)</CLToolPath>
    <CLToolExe>sembazuru.exe</CLToolExe>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
